From 978e9dcd93e266493e5b079609c4e445fb817ea3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:58:32 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 053/230] Fix web login flow and Onboarding UX, tighten test
 resilience
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Auth: remove the dev:1 fallback in production from currentAuthToken() so a
fresh browser with no session and no Telegram SDK returns null instead of a
token the server will 401. hasExternalIdentity() already treats null as
"no identity", so RequireAuth now redirects to /login instead of stalling on
a blank loading screen. The dev:1 escape hatch still works in non-production
for local development.

Onboarding: add loading skeleton, error state with retry, and empty state to
both team grids (pick-favorite and pick-more-clubs steps). Previously the
grids silently rendered nothing while teamsQuery was loading, errored, or
empty — now each state has a visible placeholder and the error state lets the
user retry.

i18n: add en/fa keys for the new onboarding states.

Tests: update guestMerge, accountDeletion and moderation to use INSERT OR
REPLACE for their team rows so they survive the new static team seed (which
inserts those same ESPN ids during migrate). Bare INSERT INTO now throws
UNIQUE on the seed row.

Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
